  "target_set_euid": "M-BGS-174",
  "root_euid": "M-BRM-VG",
  "cause": "LabActionsService stores every run-set membership as two opposing persisted directed edges: canonical run_set_member plus redundant associated_set. Native DAG v2 rejects the ten resulting two-edge cycles.",
  "effect": "Soft-delete only the ten named associated_set lineage records. Keep all objects, ten canonical run_set_member records, unrelated lineage, metadata and audit history. No hard deletion, schema reset or graph-validation relaxation.",
  "auth": "Apply only through Bloom's public owning API using an existing authorized owner-writer context after the separate destructive confirmation; no auth grants or DB bypass. Read observations used existing Kahlo reader.",
  "preconditions": [
    "Explicit destructive confirmation names this exact ten-edge repair and effect.",
    "Final writer correction deployed, preventing new associated_set rows.",
    "Re-read exact set lineage lists and exact all-ten audit/lineage selectors; require same endpoints, relationship types, active state, and preserved counterparts.",
    "Retain immutable before snapshot and request/response receipts; fail on any unexpected identity or response. After partial failure, re-read and report the exact completed subset; never automatically retry with different targets."
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Ten reverse edges no longer active; ten exact canonical membership edge IDs remain active.",
    "Every original object and all unrelated set lineage remain unchanged.",
    "Public audit records show the soft deletions under the executing owner actor.",
    "Native GET /api/dag/v2/data?start_euid=M-BRM-VG&depth=4 succeeds with actual graph data, then Kahlo graph traversal is observed. New independent errors remain explicit."
  ],
